<title>UK: Clarke sees PSBR in balance by 1999-2000.</title>
<headline>Clarke sees PSBR in balance by 1999-2000.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor Kenneth Clarke on Tuesday forecast that the UK public sector borrowing requirement (PSBR) would be broadly in balance by 1999-2000.</p>
<p>&quot;I expect the PSBR to be 26-1/2 billion stg this year. That will mean it has halved as a share of GDP over the past three years. I expect it to come down to 19 billion pounds next year and to be broadly in balance by 1999-2000,&quot; Clarke said in his budget presentation.</p>
<p>He said the pattern of decline was &quot;much better&quot; than the one in his summer economic forecast in July.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 2774</p>
